<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">tutorial</ansi>

New characters begin in a short course of rooms, their own copy of it, that
teaches the basics one lesson at a time. The way into each next room opens
when you have done what the lesson asks:

  <ansi fg="yellow">Character</ansi>  look yourself over: status, inventory, experience, conditions.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Company</ansi>    recruit two companions.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Formation</ansi>  put one in the front row and another behind.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Survival</ansi>   eat and drink, and check the weather, temperature, strain,
             and cargo. The wardens hand you food or water if you have none.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Camp</ansi>       make camp, light a fire, and rest until you are Rested.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Combat</ansi>     beat a squad of straw soldiers, which can't hurt you, and see
             how reach, interception, and re-targeting work.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Alignment</ansi>  check your company's alignment, weigh an outlaw recruit against
             it, and check your standing with the towns.
  <ansi fg="yellow">Departure</ansi>  walk out through the gate.
Your place in the course is saved, so logging out and back in picks up
where you left off (except during a replay, below).

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">tutorial</ansi>
  Show the current lesson, its goal, a checklist, and hints.

  <ansi fg="command">tutorial next</ansi>
  Move past a lesson you cannot finish, for example when both tutorial
  recruits were already claimed by an earlier character on your account,
  when you have nothing left to eat or drink (the meal is waived, the
  checks aren't), when camping isn't available, or when there's no one to
  practice against.

  <ansi fg="command">tutorial skip</ansi>
  Leave the course now, for the town. It asks you to confirm with
  <ansi fg="command">tutorial skip yes</ansi>. Skipping gives no graduation reward.
  During a replay it ends the replay instead, and you are back where
  your own character was.

  <ansi fg="command">tutorial replay</ansi>
  Run the whole course again, as often as you like, from anywhere but a
  fight. It asks you to confirm with <ansi fg="command">tutorial replay yes</ansi>.

Every command works during the course: chat, <ansi fg="command">help</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">status</ansi>, and the rest.
For every detail of how battles work, see <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.
Leaving the course, including by dying (which nothing in it can quickly
cause), finishes it for your character.

<ansi fg="yellow">Replaying the course</ansi>

A replay is a practice character: your name, race, and archetype, at
level 1 with only the starter kit, no company, and a new character's
purse. Your own character steps out of the world while you play, exactly
as if you had logged out. <ansi fg="command">online</ansi> shows you as replaying the
tutorial, and a <ansi fg="command">whisper</ansi> to your name still reaches you.

The replay ends when you graduate, skip, die, or leave the course any
other way: "You set the practice character aside," and you are your own
character again, in the same place, with the same company, camp, gear,
gold, and experience. Logging out or losing your connection ends it too;
you log back in as your own character. Nothing from a replay is kept: not
its items, experience, recruits, camp, or graduation reward.
